# Muze Next Steps

## Shareable profiles and consistent public-profile taste browsing

Product contract:

- Use one bundled static banner, `assets/shared-profile-banner.jpg`; never generate or compose a per-user image.
- The forwarded photo caption is a compact first-person public taste teaser: the user's profile emoji when present, up to five Profile Interests, available media taste labels, and at most one Favorite from each non-empty Movies/Music/Books section. It omits the display name.
- Never include Stars, private growth hints, location, age, gender, pet preference, hidden discussion state, or Watch/Listen/Read Later items in shareable copy.
- Put the opaque attributable bot link directly in the photo caption so forwarding preserves it. Profile sharing uses the existing genuinely-new external referral reward and must never stack with another referral claim.
- Reuse onboarding exactly as it works now. Existing onboarded users open the destination immediately; genuinely new users complete the unchanged onboarding flow, see its existing completion message/reply keyboard, and then automatically receive the promised profile card.
- Every other-user public profile uses the same public content and core Favorites action. Only source-specific Save/Remove, Discussions eligibility, restriction controls, and return/close navigation vary by context. The own-profile editing surface stays separate.
- Public Favorites browsing exposes only Favorite lists and stored media taste labels. It never exposes For Later lists. Compatibility/comparison remains deferred.

Implementation steps:

✔ 1. Documented the shareable-profile, referral destination, onboarding continuation, privacy, and public Favorites contract in `docs/bot-ux.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/agent-map.md`, and `docs/stars.md`.

✔ 2. Extended external referral links with a `profile_share` source and public-profile destination while retaining opaque tokens and the existing claim/reward rules; unit and Mongo integration tests cover destination persistence and non-rewarding link resolution.

✔ 3. Added shared-profile start routing and durable `pendingProfileShareCode`; existing users open immediately, while unfinished users receive normal onboarding completion before the profile.

✔ 4. Added the conditional full-width share action, focused caption service, 350,735-byte static JPEG banner delivery through the shared cache/fallback path, and compact forwarding guidance with Back. Creating it leaves the original profile and generated banner untouched.

✔ 5. Added the conditional `❤️ Favorites` action across People, Saved Profiles, discussion members, invitations, restrictions, shared links, and direct public-profile views while preserving source-specific actions.

✔ 6. Added caption-safe public Favorites hub/section views for Movies/Music/Books and stored taste labels only, with in-place Back-to-profile restoration and delete-only Close.

✔ 7. Added bilingual copy and callback/navigation recognition; `npm.cmd run validate:translations` passes for all 912 English/Persian keys.

✔ 8. Added focused unit, flow, callback-adjacent, and integration coverage for caption privacy/length/copy, complete-list gating, fallback delivery, referral destinations and non-rewarding cases, onboarding order, public Favorites, photo restoration, exact reply-keyboard restoration, in-place Save, and safe current-discussion handling; the full existing suite remains green.

✔ 9. Validation complete: translations pass, the full unit suite passes, and the integration suite including profile-share referral persistence passes. Deployment remains a separate approval-gated task.
